title: Second Emergency Decree for Economy and Finance
subtitle: Chancellor [+ chancellor +] enacts a controversial emergency decree.
new-page: true
view-if: total_bruning_time == 15 and bruning_toleration_time and (hoover_moratorium_seen or war_loans == -2) and not emergency_decree_seen and not concord_formed and not lautenbach_adopted and not bruning_sigma_time and not bruning_skibidi_time
on-arrival: emergency_decree_alt_seen = 1; ddp_right += 1; ddp_cohesion -= 1; gold_right += 3; lvp_right += 2; liberal_cooperation -= 1; bourgeois_cooperation -= 1; pro_republic -= 3; burgher_royalist += burgher_ddp*0.1; guild_royalist += guild_ddp*0.05; burgher_royalist += burgher_gold*0.1; guild_royalist += guild_gold*0.1; burgher_ddp *= 0.2; guild_ddp *= 0.9; burgher_gold *= 0.8; guild_gold *= 0.8; burgher_royalist += burgher_lvp*0.2; guild_royalist += guild_lvp*0.2; burgher_lvp *= 0.8; guild_lvp *= 0.8
tags: event
face-image: img/article48.jpg
max-visits: 1

= Second Emergency Decree for Economy and Finance

To fully eliminate the national budget deficit, the emergency decree introduces spending cuts alongside a special “crisis tax.” However, with War Loan payments paused, Askew has been able to implement these austerity measures more leniently than anticipated.

Despite being less severe than expected, the decree has sparked widespread outrage, further fueling attacks from the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> against the propertied parties that remain aligned with Askew—particularly the [? if not lvp_formed: [? if gold_exist: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> and ?]<span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?], as they're the [? if not lvp_formed and gold_exist:parties?][? if lvp_formed or not gold_exist:party?] representing the social groups most impacted by these changes. [? if not lvp_formed and not bourgeois_parliament and not liberal_parliament: The liberal parties' failure to persuade Askew to remove cuts to civil servants’ salaries and the increase in the national sales tax has strained their relationship with his government.?]

We can either continue tolerating Askew’s government or use this decree as a pretext to break with it.

# different stuff for different ddp and dvp leaders and lvp existence or propertied parliament or kvp 

- @nothing_to_do: There is nothing we can do.
- @vote_no
- @vote_yes

@nothing_to_do
view-if: marcher_toleration == 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.budget += 1;
Q.inflation -= 1.5;
Q.disfavored += 1.5;
Q.economic_growth -= 1;
Q.emergency_decree_mitigated = Q.liberal_parliament || (Q.bourgeois_parliament && !Q.lvp_formed) || Q.lvp_formed;
if (Q.emergency_decree_mitigated) {
    Q.disfavored -= 0.5;
    Q.budget -= 1;
    Q.inflation += 0.8;
    Q.economic_growth += 0.4;
    Q.burgher_ddp += 2;
    Q.guild_ddp += 1;
    Q.burgher_gold += 3;
    Q.guild_gold += 3;
    Q.landed_gold += 1;
    Q.burgher_lvp += 4;
    Q.guild_lvp += 6;
    Q.landed_lvp += 2;
    Q.burgher_royalist -= 4;
    Q.guild_royalist -= 4;
    Q.gold_left += 3;
    Q.ddp_left += 2;
    Q.ddp_cohesion += 2;
    Q.lvp_left += 3;
}
if (Q.emergency_decree_mitigated_more) {
    Q.disfavored -= 0.2;
    Q.inflation += 0.2;
    Q.economic_growth += 0.1;
    Q.burgher_ddp += 1;
    Q.guild_ddp += 1;
    Q.burgher_gold += 2;
    Q.guild_gold += 2;
    Q.landed_gold += 1;
    Q.burgher_lvp += 2;
    Q.guild_lvp += 2;
    Q.landed_lvp += 1;
    Q.burgher_royalist -= 2;
    Q.guild_royalist -= 2;
    Q.gold_left += 2;
    Q.ddp_left += 1;
    Q.lvp_left += 2;
}
!}

The emergency policy passes under emergency rules, as the Assembly is currently dissolved. The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> use this as a recruiting tool, and so do we.

[? if bourgeois_parliament and not lvp_formed and not liberal_parliament: Fortunately, the propertied parliamentary group, with their leverage over Askew, has managed to persuade him to drop the decree! The group argues that the pause in War Loan payments have made the proposed cuts unnecessary, and that Askew should tone down his austerity measures. [? if bourgeois_parliament_ddp: Furthermore, the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>'s presence in the parliamentary group has led Vice-Chancellor and Finance Minister Dietrich of the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> to personally mitigate the severity of Askew's austerity measures.?]?][? if liberal_parliament: Fortunately, the liberal parliamentary group has allowed the liberal parties to combine their leverage over Askew, and persuade him to drop the decree!, The group argues that the pause in War Loan payments have made the proposed cuts unnecessary, and that Askew should tone down his austerity measures. [? if liberal_parliament and liberal_cooperation >= 8: Furthermore, the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>'s Vice-Chancellor and Finance Minister Dietrich is able to personally mitigate the severity of Askew's austerity measures.?]?][? if lvp_formed: Fortunately, the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>, using their leverage over Askew, has successfully persuaded him to drop the decree! The group argues that the pause in War Loan payments has made the proposed cuts unnecessary and that Askew should scale back his austerity measures. [? if lvp_leader == "Lytton": Furthermore, the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>'s leader Hans Lytton is able to use his connections with Askew and the industrial community to influence his economic policy away from unrestrained austerity.?]?]

